    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "delphisci Levin papers claim extractor";
    prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-opus-5.5>.
sub:quote a prov:Entity;
    prov:hadPrimarySource <https://raw.githubusercontent.com/fractastical/delphisci/2404c437f822e1c98420130cd01e7972acf3ac57/books/levin-papers/inputs/2024-collective.txt#line=45,46>;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1038/s42003-024-06037-4>;
    <https://schema.org/text> "In other words, it is actually impossible for an anatomical decision like this to be made locally – the cells of the wound must coordinate with the remaining fragment to get information about where they are located, which way they are facing, and what other structures exist121,122, in order to make adaptive decisions about large-scale growth and form that enable regeneration of normal worms.".
